# The wizard compiles the files below byte for byte into Setup_CommandPulse.exe,
# so their line endings are part of the released artifact - not an artefact of
# the developer's machine. Without a rule here a checkout inherits
# core.autocrlf, and the same commit compiles to a different executable:
# rebuilding the v1.6.9 tag from an LF checkout and from a normal CRLF checkout
# produced 2,327,289 and 2,327,521 bytes respectively (C4C4BEC7... and
# 9419D04F...). That is why the shipped setup program could not be rebuilt from
# its own tag. eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf, so every clone, worktree and CI
# checkout feeds ISCC the same bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored binaries must never be normalised.
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
